WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 8: Home, Sweet Home.

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.760
This unit is all about homes.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:14.660
You will learn the names of homes for people and for
animals — a house, a flat, a hut, a tree house, a nest,

4
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:15.880
a hive and a hole.

5
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:22.700
You will name the rooms inside a home and the things we keep
in them, and you will compare homes from around the world.

6
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.740
You will say where things are with in,
on, under, next to, between and above,

7
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:35.540
use there is and there are to say what a home has,
and use will to promise the jobs you will do at home.

8
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:43.340
By the end you can give a tour of your own home, just like
Amal does in this unit's story, “Helping Hands at Home”.

9
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.640
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.460
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
different kinds of homes for people and animals.

11
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.620
You will also name the rooms in a home
and say what people do in each one.

12
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.740
You will also name common things at
home and say which room they belong in.

13
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.260
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:14.280
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
name, game, late, place, theme, bathroom.

15
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.400
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

16
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.800
The reading sequence includes A Poem:
“Homes” and Different Kinds of Homes.

17
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

18
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.980
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

19
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.860
The first language focus is Prepositions of Place.

20
00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.620
Prepositions of place are small
words that tell us where something is.

21
00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.560
They help you describe your home so that
another person can picture every room.

22
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.620
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

23
00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.860
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Describe a Kind of Home.

24
00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.940
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

25
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:08.500
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

26
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.400
You are ready to begin.

27
00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:16.480
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

28
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:23.320
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
